  "prefLabel": "Env-C 802.11 Exemplary natural community",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-C 802.11 “Exemplary natural community” means “exemplary natural community” as defined in RSA 217-A:3, VII, namely “a viable occurrence of a rare natural community type or a high quality example of a more common natural community type as designated by the natural heritage bureau based on community size, ecological condition, and landscape context.”\n\nSource. #14374, INTERIM, eff 8-26-25; ss by #14473 (formerly Env-C 802.09), eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES 1-19-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-c800.html"
